> This looks like an aggravated form of C343-204, and I'd imagine it'll
> be addressed by the fix for that.

     The not releasing part is covered by it.  That fix causes
non-hostile engulfers or grabbers who haven't already
released the hero to do so the next time it's their turn to
make a non-Conflict move.

     But the defunct monster aspect is different.  It's caused
by the code that makes a pet who's being hit by hero lose
some tameness and start fleeing.  The code isn't checking
whether the tame monster has just taken fatal damage.
It calls monflee, which calls release_hero, which calls
expels, which puts both the hero and the engulfer back
onto the map.  The tameness abuse matters even if the
pet has died, since in impacts revival.  (Actually, I don't
think that it does, since having the hero be responsible
for the pet's death should override its old tameness and
abuse record during corpse revival.)  The fleeing should
definitely be skipped when the pet is killed, and skipping
that will avoid calling expels and triggering this "placing
defunct monster onto map" warning.



